.TH OOBE-GXWI 1 2026-10-19 "Peios installer 0.1.13"
.SH NAME
oobe-gxwi \- Peios first-boot setup, in a browser, as GXWI's overlay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oobe-gxwi
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR ADDRESS : PORT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oobe-gxwi
presents the conversation owned by
.BR oobed (8)
as a GXWI browser overlay.
The daemon performs the privileged operations.
All connected browsers observe and modify the same conversation.
Closing a browser does not cancel a daemon job.
.PP
GXWI starts the frontend with an inherited Unix listening socket and handles
the external browser connection.
The frontend serves HTTP/2 over that socket.
For development,
.B \-\-listen
starts a direct HTTP listener without GXWI's TLS termination.
All browser assets are embedded in the executable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
.BR oobed 's
socket.
The default is
.IR /run/oobed.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " ADDRESS" : PORT
Serve here instead of on a socket handed over, for working on the page where
there is no GXWI.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of these.
.SH SECURITY
The overlay is available without normal sign-in.
Coordinate with other people using it and keep the machine on a trusted
network until setup completes.
Verify the GXWI certificate through the machine's trusted console before
entering a password.
.PP
Direct development listeners serve unencrypted HTTP.
Use synthetic credentials and an isolated environment for those listeners.
The frontend relies on GXWI for external connection security and on the
daemon's socket access controls for its MSIP connection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help, version, or normal server completion.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, missing inherited socket, or server initialization error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LISTEN_FDS
Must indicate at least one inherited descriptor when
.B \-\-listen
is absent.
The frontend takes ownership of descriptor 3 as its Unix listener.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/oobed.sock
Default conversation socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gxwid (1),
.BR installer-gxwi (1),
.BR oobed (8)
